Ja, looking at Hamin... Say Yejun's the one
who keeps everyone in line.

00:49:25.460 --> 00:49:29.660
Then Hamin... how do I say this?
[Chat: He'll guess down to the centimeter.]

00:49:29.670 --> 00:49:39.800
He seems steady. Like he'd stick to his guns,
but he's got a thoughtful side too.

00:49:39.810 --> 00:49:48.520
They've all got their own thing going.
A mix of qualities, I guess?

00:49:48.980 --> 00:49:57.720
Steady, because everybody here has
such a strong personality. In the middle...

00:49:59.080 --> 00:50:05.370
Hang on.

00:50:05.380 --> 00:50:12.900
They really stand out. Look at their hair,
their eye colors, all that. But Hamin...

00:50:12.910 --> 00:50:16.140
He's steady. Less is more, you know?

00:50:16.150 --> 00:50:23.140
So he can fit with a lot of different styles
and it wouldn't feel out of place.

00:50:25.860 --> 00:50:29.560
This is hard to put into words. Hamin...

00:50:29.570 --> 00:50:37.760
Put him with anyone
and I think they'd have good chemistry.

00:50:37.770 --> 00:50:45.300
I mean, I'm sure there's a name
for each pairing in the group.

00:50:45.310 --> 00:50:50.260
But I feel like Hamin would work
with any of them.

00:50:51.900 --> 00:50:56.960
He doesn't need to stand out on his own.
It's more like they click. What's the word?

00:51:00.260 --> 00:51:07.560
Uh... I think he makes it easier
for everyone to gel.

00:51:10.040 --> 00:51:17.880
He might look standoffish at first,
but he seems easygoing. Easygoing.

00:51:20.440 --> 00:51:28.340
And by easygoing, I mean
he's still got his own convictions.

00:51:30.100 --> 00:51:36.940
But I bet he's good at adapting.
He'd back up the others instead of showing off.

00:51:36.950 --> 00:51:40.770
Like he's the secret ingredient.
That's kind of his role.

00:51:40.780 --> 00:51:43.280
[Chat: Are you a member? LOL]

00:51:45.580 --> 00:51:51.220
He supports them, but that doesn't mean
he just fades into the background.

00:51:52.900 --> 00:51:57.990
No. It's more like
he brings out the chemistry.

00:51:58.000 --> 00:52:00.400
[Chat: Did you watch their videos first? LOL]

00:52:00.410 --> 00:52:09.980
No, I seriously didn't watch their videos.
I was saving my first taste for someday.

00:52:09.990 --> 00:52:16.440
I know they do livestreams and stuff.
I just didn't watch them.

00:52:17.240 --> 00:52:19.260
[Reading chat] “Hamin's role?”
Right.

00:52:21.220 --> 00:52:27.120
For his role... well, first off...

00:52:28.340 --> 00:52:36.880
Sorry, but I bet he's got an amazing voice.
I haven't called anyone a standout vocalist yet.

00:52:36.890 --> 00:52:39.540
An incredible singer and a good dancer.

00:52:41.300 --> 00:52:44.680
Man, this is going to be fun.

00:52:48.120 --> 00:52:54.840
He feels like... white. White?
Yeah, that's the vibe.

00:52:55.120 --> 00:52:58.860
He gives off best-vocalist vibes.
That's my impression.

00:52:58.870 --> 00:53:02.820
A white Doberman. That's it.

00:53:03.860 --> 00:53:15.180
He seems like he loves PLAVE as a group
more than anyone.

00:53:15.190 --> 00:53:17.870
[Chat: Singing AND dancing?
That's overpowered.]

00:53:17.880 --> 00:53:23.340
Dobermans are loyal, right?
He seems loyal in a protective way.

00:53:23.350 --> 00:53:27.520
Oh, hi, Roda!

00:53:30.560 --> 00:53:34.840
Looking at him, that's exactly it.
Though with Hamin...

00:53:34.850 --> 00:53:41.040
I feel like all I've said is “solid support.”
Even I think that's a little unsatisfying.

00:53:43.800 --> 00:53:48.040
You want me to guess their animal symbols?
They have animal symbols?

00:53:49.720 --> 00:53:50.700
Huh? Hamin...

00:53:53.380 --> 00:53:59.480
Just going off their looks,
Noah...

00:53:59.490 --> 00:54:01.150
[Chat: Good instincts or not?]

00:54:01.160 --> 00:54:05.100
gives me Pegasus vibes.

00:54:07.320 --> 00:54:10.300
Doesn't Bamby already have
the whole Bambi thing?

00:54:14.560 --> 00:54:16.400
They have official animals?

00:54:17.340 --> 00:54:19.840
Hi! Welcome back. It's been a while.

00:54:19.850 --> 00:54:28.760
Hamin... a black horse?
Or a crow?

00:54:29.740 --> 00:54:31.280
I doubt they'd pick a crow.

00:54:32.940 --> 00:54:35.780
[Reading chat] “How princely is he
if you went with Pegasus?”

00:54:35.790 --> 00:54:39.840
Black horse, crow, Doberman.
That's the vibe I get.

00:54:43.320 --> 00:54:49.440
And Yejun. He's totally a border collie to me,
but you said they have animal symbols...

00:54:50.900 --> 00:54:52.680
An animal symbol.

00:54:55.500 --> 00:54:58.840
That's cool. Did you know crows
are really smart?

00:55:02.420 --> 00:55:04.680
But I doubt that's what they'd pick.

00:55:06.800 --> 00:55:16.060
I can't get border collie out of my head
for Yejun. But it's not a border collie, right?

00:55:16.070 --> 00:55:19.330
[Chat: Look at our usernames for a clue.]

00:55:19.340 --> 00:55:21.040
It's not a border collie, is it?

00:55:22.320 --> 00:55:28.900
Yejun... Hamin... Yejun.
Something blue. Like something blue-backed...

00:55:28.910 --> 00:55:32.180
White... It can't be a mackerel, right?

00:55:33.340 --> 00:55:37.060
A dolphin? Oh!
He does have a dolphin vibe, too.

00:55:37.070 --> 00:55:42.160
Huh? It could still be a border collie.
It's in your username?

00:55:43.320 --> 00:55:44.920
Wait, there's a dolphin?

00:55:45.600 --> 00:55:50.940
Huh? Really?
Then I think Yejun's a dolphin.

00:55:52.600 --> 00:55:53.400
Dolphin.

00:55:54.900 --> 00:55:58.580
I was thinking along the lines
of a blue-backed fish, and dolphin came to mind.

00:56:00.060 --> 00:56:01.720
Keep border collie on the list.

00:56:03.380 --> 00:56:07.840
Hang on. Pegasus.
Noah: Pegasus. Final answer.

00:56:07.850 --> 00:56:11.540
How did I get to blue-backed fish?
Well, he's kind of blue here.

00:56:11.550 --> 00:56:14.180
Oh, I missed the hint in chat just now.

00:56:17.020 --> 00:56:21.360
For Bamby, isn't there an animal called Bambi?
It fits his look, too.

00:56:22.320 --> 00:56:25.180
Is Bamby's animal maybe Bambi?

00:56:26.980 --> 00:56:32.660
Pink Chihuahua, little mutt.
He's the GOAT of being cute.

00:56:32.670 --> 00:56:38.420
Wait, is it not a bambi?
Is there an animal called a dambi?

00:56:39.680 --> 00:56:42.400
Isn't a bambi a kind of deer?

00:56:46.960 --> 00:56:48.260
Is it Bambi?

00:56:49.780 --> 00:56:51.600
Bambi is a character?

00:56:52.680 --> 00:56:54.760
Then I'll go with spotted deer.

00:56:55.000 --> 00:56:58.650
[Chat: Wait till you find out Noah's animal.
You might be disappointed.]

00:56:59.780 --> 00:57:02.440
I'm putting down spotted deer.

00:57:04.040 --> 00:57:06.440
You're saying Pegasus is a pretty good guess?

00:57:06.450 --> 00:57:16.680
Then maybe Pegasus or a unicorn.
Something like that.

00:57:19.200 --> 00:57:21.600
Eunho's definitely a wolf.

00:57:27.500 --> 00:57:31.220
Should I think about yours a little more?
If not a wolf, what else could it be?

00:57:31.230 --> 00:57:41.620
Ah, he's a wolf. A wolf.
Definitely a wolf.

00:57:43.180 --> 00:57:49.840
Hamin: black horse... No, Doberman is right.
He's got that Doberman look.

00:57:50.560 --> 00:57:52.780
I don't think it's a crow.

00:57:52.790 --> 00:57:55.200
[Chat: Well, it does have four legs. LOL]

00:57:56.900 --> 00:58:01.980
I feel like the fans would go, “What?
A crow?!” and scold me. Pass.

00:58:11.820 --> 00:58:15.440
There's a Dolphin Duo? Wait,
does that make this one an orca?

00:58:17.420 --> 00:58:19.840
If there's a Dolphin Duo... an orca?

00:58:22.420 --> 00:58:31.100
He seems like someone
who sticks to his own opinions. Am I right?

00:58:34.620 --> 00:58:43.060
Those two seem like they'd really click.
Yejun and Hamin, right?

00:58:43.320 --> 00:58:45.860
[Reading chat] “Why are you so nervous?”

00:58:45.870 --> 00:58:47.900
You all just love to tease me.

00:58:47.940 --> 00:58:53.120
Ah, but now I want to know too!
You got me curious.

00:58:54.220 --> 00:58:59.320
I think that's enough for now.
I've got more to taste, after all.

00:59:00.820 --> 00:59:05.640
So... aha. Now I'm curious too.

00:59:07.460 --> 00:59:12.700
Ja, let's leave it there
and see what else we've got.

00:59:12.710 --> 00:59:14.820
Oh, hey, I need to look at this.

00:59:14.830 --> 00:59:16.950
[Chat: Time to grade your guesses!]

00:59:16.960 --> 00:59:19.550
[Reading chat] “Two wrong, three right?”

00:59:22.480 --> 00:59:26.540
Yejun. “Producer”? Wait, what?

00:59:30.880 --> 00:59:32.640
Leader! Ah!

00:59:32.650 --> 00:59:34.730
[Chat: Everyone, grab a stick! LOL]

00:59:34.740 --> 00:59:39.900
He keeps the team in line! I said “a leader who
isn't the leader.” He really IS the leader!

00:59:42.260 --> 00:59:43.180
Leader.

00:59:45.900 --> 00:59:53.260
Hang on. You're saying he's the leader,
a main vocalist, AND a producer?

00:59:55.000 --> 00:59:58.260
They write and compose
their own songs?

00:59:58.270 --> 01:00:03.440
No, but seriously... that's fucking cool.

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:07.710
[Chat: Producers write, compose, arrange,
and direct recording sessions.]

01:00:07.720 --> 01:00:15.300
He does everything. And he's not
the only one who does everything?

01:00:16.200 --> 01:00:19.080
Ah, “maebo.” Main vocalist.

01:00:21.620 --> 01:00:25.040
Noah. Ja, the first prince.

01:00:25.050 --> 01:00:27.240
I said that. It's not on the screen.

01:00:27.250 --> 01:00:34.920
Main vocalist. I said he could rap and sing.
Or rather, sing and rap. Right?

01:00:37.980 --> 01:00:42.400
So main vocalist and producing too.

01:00:42.410 --> 01:00:46.080
Wait, can he rap too?
He seems like he'd be good at everything.

01:00:46.090 --> 01:00:47.020
[Chat: He can!]

01:00:47.030 --> 01:00:50.840
Ja. Oh, dancer.

01:00:50.850 --> 01:00:54.550
[On screen: Bamby — main dancer,
vocals, choreographer]

01:00:54.560 --> 01:00:58.040
That's insane. That's insane.

01:00:59.740 --> 01:01:03.360
Vocals AND choreography?

01:01:05.660 --> 01:01:07.060
A choreographer?

01:01:09.060 --> 01:01:14.180
I said he gave off dancer vibes.
I didn't get as far as choreographer.

01:01:16.860 --> 01:01:19.660
Wait, I got that right!

01:01:19.900 --> 01:01:22.720
What the hell? I forgot I'd even said that.

01:01:22.730 --> 01:01:25.960
[Highlighted note: Total dancer energy
+ stronger on vocals]

01:01:25.970 --> 01:01:27.530
[Chat: He hits high notes too.]

01:01:27.540 --> 01:01:32.660
No way. But I did think
he'd be a good dancer.

01:01:32.670 --> 01:01:38.480
Like, clothes flying, hitting each beat.
That K-pop idol precision.

01:01:38.490 --> 01:01:44.560
I could picture those sharp stops.
Really clean, controlled moves.

01:01:44.570 --> 01:01:45.610
[Chat: Nailed Bamby.]

01:01:45.620 --> 01:01:52.200
I figured he'd be good, but he went
from dancer to choreographer.

01:01:52.210 --> 01:01:55.860
Not just the main dancer. A choreographer!
His lines really are beautiful.

01:01:55.870 --> 01:02:02.480
If I get the chance, I should do a stream
where I learn PLAVE choreography.

01:02:02.490 --> 01:02:07.500
Ja, Eunho. Main rapper. Main rapper.

01:02:08.820 --> 01:02:13.240
Vocals and producer. Wow. Come on.

01:02:15.320 --> 01:02:16.080
That's insane.

01:02:18.000 --> 01:02:20.860
Imagine how much feedback
they trade while producing.

01:02:22.180 --> 01:02:24.460
Vocals... no, rapper, right.

01:02:25.500 --> 01:02:29.820
Did I not say it here? Oh, I did:
“main dancer, rapper.” Right.

01:02:31.100 --> 01:02:39.820
I really thought he'd be good.
Eunho just looked the part. I get it.

01:02:41.200 --> 01:02:46.080
I had heard that they do their own production.

01:02:46.090 --> 01:02:50.420
Why? My older sister is a huge PLAVE fan.

01:02:53.400 --> 01:02:58.980
She kept telling me, “Try them on stream.”
Then, “Make a whole meal of it on stream.”

01:03:00.340 --> 01:03:03.560
That's what she'd tell me. She's over there.

01:03:03.570 --> 01:03:09.340
Yejun, Noah, and Eunho make the music,
and Bamby and Hamin make the dances? Solid.

01:03:12.740 --> 01:03:20.240
But I really didn't watch their content. Even
when she'd tell me stuff, I tried not to listen.

01:03:20.250 --> 01:03:23.460
Why? It wouldn't be as fun
when I finally dug in like this.

01:03:23.470 --> 01:03:29.980
So I avoided whatever I could.
I knew I'd get around to it someday.

01:03:29.990 --> 01:03:35.320
Ja, main dancer. Ooh, lead rapper.

01:03:35.330 --> 01:03:38.720
Those roles are cool. Choreographer?

01:03:38.730 --> 01:03:40.530
[On screen: Hamin]

01:03:40.540 --> 01:03:41.820
Another choreographer?

01:03:41.830 --> 01:03:45.310
[Chat: The swimming guess gave me chills.]

01:03:45.320 --> 01:03:49.100
My swimming guess gave you chills?

01:03:52.820 --> 01:03:54.760
Eunho's good at swimming?

01:03:56.420 --> 01:04:01.140
[Reading chat] “Blood relatives don't listen.”
True. Neither me nor my sister listens.

01:04:03.680 --> 01:04:09.790
We give each other unsolicited life advice,
and neither of us takes it.

01:04:09.799 --> 01:04:15.720
“Uh-huh. Sure. Got it.”
Even this Chuseok it was like that.

01:04:18.480 --> 01:04:20.500
Yeah, exactly.

01:04:20.510 --> 01:04:23.590
[Chat: My little sibling ignores
my PLAVE pitches too.]

01:04:25.359 --> 01:04:29.500
I thought it'd be fun to get into them
for the first time with you all on stream.

01:04:29.520 --> 01:04:33.520
Huh, now I'm suddenly curious. Ja, so...

01:04:34.460 --> 01:04:38.560
Hang on. Let's crop off the side here.

01:04:40.140 --> 01:04:41.460
I'll zoom in on this part.

01:04:58.000 --> 01:05:01.390
They mentioned it in their introductions?

01:05:01.400 --> 01:05:03.400
There. “Member chemistry.”

01:05:05.580 --> 01:05:06.700
Oh!

01:05:09.540 --> 01:05:13.380
Let's make it easier to see.

01:05:15.200 --> 01:05:21.200
Whoa, there are a lot. This is fun.
Where's the Dolphin Duo?

01:05:25.400 --> 01:05:27.800
Ja... oh, the oldest-member duo.

01:05:27.810 --> 01:05:29.610
[On screen: Yejun & Noah]

01:05:29.620 --> 01:05:32.860
Berry Duo. This is fun.
[On screen: Yejun & Bamby]

01:05:33.480 --> 01:05:37.300
Puppy Duo. Yejun and Eunho.

01:05:37.310 --> 01:05:41.860
Oh, the border collie meets the wolf.

01:05:41.870 --> 01:05:44.740
I guessed the animals...
[Reading chat] “No Dolphin Duo?”

01:05:45.440 --> 01:05:48.380
Aw, too bad. What is the Dolphin Duo, then?

01:05:51.640 --> 01:05:57.180
Ye Line. Ye Line is Yejun and Hamin.

01:05:57.190 --> 01:06:01.620
Oh, is it Ye Line because Hamin's
on Yejun's side?

01:06:02.260 --> 01:06:07.020
Noah's Line. Pretty Line.
Oh, is it “pretty”?

01:06:09.800 --> 01:06:16.920
Oh, that's right? Ah, Yejun's line.
Then there's a bit of a rivalry, huh?

01:06:16.930 --> 01:06:18.600
Eunho and Noah are Noah's Line.

01:06:23.500 --> 01:06:33.660
So Bamby's caught in the middle. Two against
two, and he's the one who gets squished.

01:06:33.670 --> 01:06:37.840
Is “Pretty Line” a thing too?

01:06:40.460 --> 01:06:43.400
Oh, so to balance them out, there's Bam Line.

01:06:44.740 --> 01:06:47.200
Oh! That's hilarious.

01:06:50.520 --> 01:06:51.420
“Traits”...

01:06:54.200 --> 01:06:58.840
Bam Line is just Bamby?
So he's right in the middle.

01:06:58.850 --> 01:07:00.780
Yataz?

01:07:00.790 --> 01:07:07.060
There's so much to read here.

01:07:07.070 --> 01:07:13.640
Yataz, Noah's Line, Puppy Duo, Dance Duo.
Oh, Bamby and Hamin.

01:07:15.420 --> 01:07:21.280
Bamby wants PLLI to be in Bam Line?
That would be so reassuring.

01:07:21.290 --> 01:07:24.800
[Chat: Yataz comes from “Hey! Hop on!”
in the motorcycle MV scene.]

01:07:25.760 --> 01:07:30.980
Oh, Yataz is from riding a motorcycle
in the MV. [On screen: Bamby & Eunho]

01:07:30.990 --> 01:07:34.480
Now I want to see that music video.

01:07:35.280 --> 01:07:38.340
Yataz... what even is that?

01:07:39.280 --> 01:07:45.940
I fucking love that. I really do.
Yataz.

01:07:45.950 --> 01:07:50.040
Man, that really got me just now.

05:57:29.440 --> 05:57:31.750
We've watched Watch Me Woo. RIZZ?

05:57:31.760 --> 05:57:34.270
Wait, what's this? Is this RIZZ?

05:57:34.280 --> 05:57:39.070
RIZZ is the one to watch, right?
Traditional-style RIZZ, then the solo stages.

05:57:39.080 --> 05:57:44.030
Hang on. If I'm being honest...

05:57:45.760 --> 05:57:52.830
I figured a lot of PLLI would show up
if I did a PLAVE watch-along.

05:57:52.840 --> 05:57:56.548
But I worried: what if my reactions
weren't fun to watch?

05:57:56.558 --> 05:58:01.110
Turns out the worries go away
as soon as you actually do it.

05:58:01.120 --> 05:58:04.990
Just do it. I'm eating this up.
I think I'm having the most fun here.

05:58:05.000 --> 05:58:08.270
I haven't heard the original
version of RIZZ yet?

05:58:08.280 --> 05:58:12.468
Okay, original RIZZ first.

05:58:12.478 --> 05:58:17.548
I was worried it might come off as forced.

05:58:17.558 --> 05:58:23.110
You know, going “Oh, wow!”
just because PLLI are watching.

05:58:23.120 --> 05:58:28.350
I was afraid it'd sound like
I was trying too hard.

05:58:28.360 --> 05:58:33.430
I was nervous, but what was I thinking?
This is fun as hell.

05:58:33.440 --> 05:58:36.628
Which one should I watch?

05:58:36.638 --> 05:58:39.138
The third one? The third one...

05:58:41.600 --> 05:58:43.000
What the...

05:59:13.840 --> 05:59:16.670
This was last year?

05:59:16.680 --> 05:59:19.070
For concerts, this is better.

05:59:41.280 --> 05:59:43.600
Whoa, cupcake!

05:59:57.160 --> 05:59:58.400
Wow.

06:00:03.120 --> 06:00:04.350
Wow!

06:00:06.680 --> 06:00:10.310
This is the “Bburinkle Chicken” song?
I had some today.

06:00:10.320 --> 06:00:15.390
My birthday was recently,
so I got a coupon for chicken.

06:00:15.400 --> 06:00:18.230
I picked Bburinkle Chicken today.

06:00:18.240 --> 06:00:22.240
I guess it was meant to be.
I ate it on the day I'm doing this!

06:00:22.250 --> 06:00:27.000
[The “freaky, cheeky, freaky” part
sounds like “Bburinkle Chicken.”]

06:00:28.558 --> 06:00:31.558
Let's hear where the Bburinkle part is.

06:00:39.040 --> 06:00:41.400
Whoa, what's with that body roll?

06:00:49.478 --> 06:00:51.478
Oh, this is insane.

06:00:53.680 --> 06:00:55.150
That's insane.

06:01:07.280 --> 06:01:10.000
No, are you kidding me?

06:01:24.280 --> 06:01:26.780
Why do my cheeks hurt?

06:01:31.920 --> 06:01:33.920
I'm losing it.

06:01:49.558 --> 06:01:52.058
Oh, Bburinkle Chicken!

06:02:04.400 --> 06:02:08.190
I asked for sexy songs, and PLLI went,
“Bburinkle Chicken.”

06:02:08.200 --> 06:02:11.070
That's fucking hilarious. And next up...

06:02:11.080 --> 06:02:15.080
So this is the “Korean food” version
of Bburinkle Chicken?

06:02:24.080 --> 06:02:26.430
Oh! So that's what they mean by “it hits.”

06:02:26.440 --> 06:02:29.070
This is fucking insane.

06:02:29.080 --> 06:02:31.080
Seriously.

06:02:35.638 --> 06:02:40.310
Wait. Is this the original choreography?

06:02:40.320 --> 06:02:43.468
Is this how the dance originally goes?

06:02:43.478 --> 06:02:44.950
Huh?

06:02:45.200 --> 06:02:48.800
They changed it, right?

06:02:50.080 --> 06:02:52.750
It's so fucking good.

06:02:52.760 --> 06:02:57.150
So fucking good. It's unreal.

06:02:57.160 --> 06:03:01.110
If the dance had looked like this earlier,
I would've liked it even more.

06:03:01.120 --> 06:03:03.600
But... wow.

06:03:07.320 --> 06:03:10.000
That's so fucking cool.

06:03:10.640 --> 06:03:11.700
Wow!

06:03:26.520 --> 06:03:30.390
They're so fucking good at this.

06:03:30.400 --> 06:03:34.100
[Reading chat] Choi Junyoung
oversaw this version of the choreo?

06:03:35.558 --> 06:03:38.500
Of course. A K-pop choreography god.

06:03:59.040 --> 06:04:02.030
Ah, I love this.

06:04:02.040 --> 06:04:04.500
It's so good.

06:04:07.120 --> 06:04:10.100
Eunho's voice makes it even better, right?

06:04:10.120 --> 06:04:12.868
Oh, that Bburinkle Chicken...

06:04:12.878 --> 06:04:16.110
Bet you didn't know sales went up.

06:04:16.120 --> 06:04:18.200
This is insane.

06:04:24.000 --> 06:04:27.000
[Reading chat] Eunho's voice
is a cheat code for pop songs?

06:04:30.280 --> 06:04:31.600
Whoa.

06:04:46.638 --> 06:04:50.200
Whoa, I just had the same reaction
as a PLLI in the audience?

06:05:06.478 --> 06:05:10.000
Wow. Seriously...

06:05:11.160 --> 06:05:14.199
And I mean this as the highest praise:

06:05:14.200 --> 06:05:18.910
Who even are you people? Seriously.

06:05:18.920 --> 06:05:20.500
Hello?!

06:05:20.840 --> 06:05:22.250
Wow. Seriously.

06:05:23.798 --> 06:05:28.708
Earlier... what was it again?
What did someone write in chat earlier?

06:05:28.718 --> 06:05:30.628
I can't even talk.

06:05:30.638 --> 06:05:34.270
Someone said they'd get banned
for saying what they really thought.

06:05:36.400 --> 06:05:38.390
Now I get what they meant.

06:05:38.400 --> 06:05:42.310
If I said everything on my mind,
PLLI might drag me for it.

06:05:42.320 --> 06:05:45.390
CHZZK could ban me. Seriously.
[The original streaming site]

06:05:45.400 --> 06:05:47.948
[Chat: “That was me.”]
Ah, I saw that. But...

06:05:47.958 --> 06:05:51.070
No, I don't think they'd drag me. Why?

06:05:51.080 --> 06:05:52.670
You'd all go just as far.

06:05:52.680 --> 06:05:55.199
Oh, Midpepper-nim. That person. Exactly.

06:05:55.200 --> 06:06:00.400
[Chat: “We PLLIs joke we'll all end up
in Cheongju Women's Prison. LOL.”]

06:06:07.360 --> 06:06:10.510
But if I'd heard that at the start,

06:06:10.520 --> 06:06:15.550
I'd have thought, “What could possibly
be that intense?”

06:06:17.478 --> 06:06:21.190
That's what I would've said. But, wow...

06:06:27.040 --> 06:06:29.468
Fuck, that's so cool.

06:06:29.478 --> 06:06:33.350
If this is how I react as a guy...

06:06:33.360 --> 06:06:37.750
I mean, it makes me think. On one hand...

06:06:39.558 --> 06:06:42.110
...it's a shame I'm not a female fan.

06:06:42.120 --> 06:06:46.100
...on the other hand, I'm relieved I'm not.

06:06:46.110 --> 06:06:47.700
Wow, this...

06:06:47.798 --> 06:06:50.230
This should be a national treasure.

06:06:53.798 --> 06:06:58.708
Everyone, PLAVE must be declared
a national treasure!

06:06:58.718 --> 06:07:01.390
Okay, that's my little outburst. Ja, next.

06:07:01.400 --> 06:07:03.000
That's it for this one.

06:07:05.600 --> 06:07:08.390
A few people fainted? I can believe it.

06:07:08.400 --> 06:07:14.430
There's a lot here that's bad for your heart,
one way or another.

06:07:14.440 --> 06:07:16.708
How are you supposed to cope?

06:07:16.718 --> 06:07:21.628
The outfits and concepts change so fast,
you can't even brace yourself.

06:07:21.638 --> 06:07:24.468
Other idols take a break
to change outfits.

06:07:24.478 --> 06:07:29.548
You can sit there and guess,
“Oh, maybe this is the next song.”

06:07:29.558 --> 06:07:32.999
You have time to do that.

06:07:33.000 --> 06:07:38.468
With PLAVE, honestly,
once they've caught their breath,

06:07:38.478 --> 06:07:41.830
and they're good to go again,

06:07:41.840 --> 06:07:45.830
everything can just change, like that.

06:07:45.840 --> 06:07:47.430
It's insane.

06:07:47.440 --> 06:07:51.500
And if you scream a lot, you get dizzy.

06:08:12.400 --> 06:08:15.390
Getting a headache at their concert?
That's not weird at all.

06:08:15.400 --> 06:08:18.390
My head hurts right now.

06:08:18.400 --> 06:08:23.030
I really didn't think I'd react like this. Wow...

06:08:23.040 --> 06:08:26.110
The dancing is delicious.
The performances are delicious.

06:08:26.120 --> 06:08:29.708
They sound great live. And for starters...

06:08:29.718 --> 06:08:32.110
They're gorgeous. But the dancing...

06:08:32.120 --> 06:08:37.590
I'm just eating it up. The way the dance
builds and tells a story...

06:08:37.600 --> 06:08:42.110
The way it works in their lore...
It's all so good.

06:08:42.120 --> 06:08:45.500
Oh, the princess! Absolute god.

06:08:46.760 --> 06:08:50.750
But Bamby is also...

06:08:50.760 --> 06:08:52.468
delicious. Wait, that sounds...

06:08:52.478 --> 06:08:55.390
weird when I say it like that.
I mean he's cool.

06:08:55.400 --> 06:08:57.548
Honestly, they're all cool.

06:08:57.558 --> 06:09:01.200
Eunho, Yejun, Hamin...

06:09:14.200 --> 06:09:16.468
“The solos were so good, I'm dying.”

06:09:16.478 --> 06:09:19.910
Should I watch this one? It's in 4K.

06:09:24.878 --> 06:09:28.000
[Voice in clip] Oh, that's why the band...

06:09:29.160 --> 06:09:32.000
[Voice in clip] Oh, the dancers up front...

06:09:35.600 --> 06:09:39.230
Look at them screaming.

06:09:39.240 --> 06:09:43.590
How could you not scream too?

06:09:43.600 --> 06:09:48.300
[Voice in clip] Oh, that's why the band...
Oh, the dancers up front...

06:10:05.240 --> 06:10:10.500
Wow, that hair. Holy shit.
Look how sexy he is.

06:10:13.798 --> 06:10:16.000
Wait a second.

06:10:21.478 --> 06:10:24.599
Oh, no one expected a solo stage,
so everyone was shocked?

06:10:24.600 --> 06:10:28.199
And that was the new hairstyle reveal?

06:10:28.200 --> 06:10:33.600
Look, a solo stage.
Yejun told them to be quiet?

06:10:38.000 --> 06:10:41.910
Wait, it was Yejun's birthday? The 12th?

06:10:41.920 --> 06:10:45.590
Mine's a day earlier. I'm on the 11th.

06:10:45.600 --> 06:10:48.030
“Trade birthdays?” That's what they said.

06:10:48.040 --> 06:10:50.150
Ah, maybe it's better this way.

06:10:50.160 --> 06:10:53.200
The 12th. Good thing it's not my birthday.

06:10:55.798 --> 06:11:00.800
But I'm never going to forget
Yejun's birthday now.

06:11:01.200 --> 06:11:05.600
The day after my birthday
is PLAVE Yejun's birthday?

06:11:10.840 --> 06:11:13.400
Wait, he had already started?

06:11:21.200 --> 06:11:24.300
He started a cappella?

06:11:30.680 --> 06:11:35.230
He's murdering PLLI out here.
Hold on...

06:11:35.240 --> 06:11:37.628
[Fakes an emergency call]
Uh, hello?

06:11:37.638 --> 06:11:42.990
Yes, I'm at the concert, and...

06:11:43.000 --> 06:11:45.948
There's a terrorist here. Yes.

06:11:45.958 --> 06:11:47.788
People are screaming.

06:11:47.798 --> 06:11:50.510
Yes. Yes. It's been a while,

06:11:50.520 --> 06:11:53.590
but every time I hear this, it's chaos.
I'm not kidding.

06:11:56.680 --> 06:12:00.628
Yes, I'm in the concert venue bathroom.

06:12:00.638 --> 06:12:04.200
No, seriously. It's crazy here.

06:12:21.958 --> 06:12:24.708
Oh, wait a second.

06:12:45.840 --> 06:12:48.200
God tier!

06:12:53.680 --> 06:12:55.600
Holy shit.

06:12:56.920 --> 06:12:59.200
Ah, fuck.

06:13:08.080 --> 06:13:12.868
Hold on. Hold on...

06:13:12.878 --> 06:13:14.948
Why are you trying to seduce me?!

06:13:14.958 --> 06:13:18.200
Wait a second. Seriously...

06:13:21.080 --> 06:13:24.150
No, I mean... Seriously.

06:13:24.160 --> 06:13:27.868
I'm not into guys, okay?

06:13:27.878 --> 06:13:30.350
But this... This is insane.

06:13:30.360 --> 06:13:32.750
What am I supposed to do? Everyone...

06:13:32.760 --> 06:13:36.510
Wow, I just...

06:13:36.520 --> 06:13:39.270
This is killing me.

06:13:39.280 --> 06:13:42.300
Seriously, this...

06:13:46.638 --> 06:13:50.000
[Chat: “It's not gay if it's PLAVE.”]
I agree.

06:14:20.000 --> 06:14:22.600
The shrug?

06:14:35.160 --> 06:14:38.200
Fuck, he's handsome.

06:14:39.878 --> 06:14:43.000
He's so damn sexy. [Laughs]

06:15:13.638 --> 06:15:16.070
Wow, this...

06:15:16.080 --> 06:15:19.788
Hang on. No, this is...

06:15:19.798 --> 06:15:23.628
I'm not joking around here.

06:15:23.638 --> 06:15:26.510
Let me watch to the end first.

06:15:26.520 --> 06:15:30.100
Wow. This doesn't make sense.

06:15:48.520 --> 06:15:52.788
Fuck, he's handsome.

06:15:52.798 --> 06:15:54.990
Isn't he just a genius?

06:15:55.000 --> 06:15:59.500
A visual genius, too. He can do it all.

06:16:21.080 --> 06:16:24.600
Wait, it's in black and white?

06:16:28.798 --> 06:16:31.600
Is it raining? Oh...

06:16:37.798 --> 06:16:40.468
Hold on. Seriously, hold on.

06:16:40.478 --> 06:16:44.230
Ja, everyone, bathroom break.

06:16:44.240 --> 06:16:47.510
I can't do this. Ja, here's what
I was going to say earlier:

06:16:47.520 --> 06:16:50.310
I'd need a diaper to go to their concert.

06:16:50.320 --> 06:16:54.190
I'm not kidding. I mean it.

06:16:54.200 --> 06:16:55.700
Seriously.

06:16:55.878 --> 06:16:59.000
This is unreal.

06:17:01.280 --> 06:17:04.800
I'll put on DASH.

06:17:06.360 --> 06:17:09.510
The music video? The performance?

06:17:09.520 --> 06:17:12.390
I'll leave the music video on.

06:17:12.400 --> 06:17:14.519
This is unreal.

06:17:14.520 --> 06:17:17.500
I'll go sort this out peacefully. Yeah.

06:19:39.360 --> 06:19:43.110
Hang on. Oh, thanks for the link
to the YouTube Short!

06:19:45.160 --> 06:19:48.110
[In the Short] I was in a hurry.
[Caption: Have you dash-ed?]

06:19:48.120 --> 06:19:49.718
[In the Short] Why? Why? Why?

06:19:49.719 --> 06:19:50.650
Why?

06:19:50.798 --> 06:19:54.700
[In the Short] “So... ah, I can't go on
like this. Hang on a second.”

06:19:54.920 --> 06:19:57.940
He'll go touch up his makeup.
[Caption: Princess's bathroom issue]

06:19:57.958 --> 06:20:01.600
[In the Short] That's exactly how
you end up looking like the culprit.

06:20:02.520 --> 06:20:04.100
[In the Short] That's the culprit!

06:20:04.240 --> 06:20:07.500
[In the Short] Are you back?
(Noah) Ah, earlier...

06:20:08.280 --> 06:20:12.540
[In the Short] Ah, I was...
I was really in a hurry.

06:20:13.000 --> 06:20:15.950
[Caption: Somehow used to Da-sheeeeeeee]

06:20:16.000 --> 06:20:19.600
[Caption: March 17, 2025;
Bamby-Squirrel Bathroom Issue]

06:20:19.638 --> 06:20:21.100
Did you DASHeee?

06:20:21.160 --> 06:20:23.830
Oh, so there's a meme about this?

06:20:23.840 --> 06:20:27.200
[In the Short, riffing on DASH lyrics]
Has the revolution sheeestarted?

06:20:28.000 --> 06:20:31.548
No. What? That's hilarious.

06:20:31.558 --> 06:20:35.070
[In the Short] Hyung, what
“revolution sheeeestarting”?!

06:20:35.080 --> 06:20:37.100
Did you dasheeeee?

06:20:38.000 --> 06:20:41.548
[Caption: Little Berry Brother
had learned something weird]

06:20:41.600 --> 06:20:44.110
Wow. So earlier, I actually...

06:20:44.120 --> 06:20:49.650
Before I watched DASH,
I had a little DASH break myself.
